From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotschmoe <isaac@mass-engineering.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] misc: armchina-npu: sky1: use the ACPI device for _ADR-only
 NPU cores

Under ACPI, sky1_npu_probe() looks up each CRE* child of the NPU with
bus_find_device_by_fwnode(&platform_bus_type, ...) and passes the result
to pm_runtime_enable(). The Minisforum MS-R1 firmware declares CRE0-CRE2
with _ADR only, so ACPI creates no platform device for them, the lookup
returns NULL, and the probe oopses; with CONFIG_PANIC_ON_OOPS the board
resets as soon as udev loads the module. On ACPI boots this was the only
driver that kept the MS-R1 from coming up.

When a core has no platform device, bind its ACPI device to itself and
use that device, as deepin's kernel and Arm China's Compass driver do.
The binding is kept across module reloads. Also disable the cores'
runtime PM in remove(), as the probe error path already does, so a
reload does not warn about an unbalanced pm_runtime_enable().

Tested on an MS-R1 with acpi=force: the driver probes with 3 cores,
each core powers up (D0) and back down (D3cold) through its power
resource, devfreq registers, and three unload/reload cycles are clean.
DT boots do not take this path.

Signed-off-by: hotschmoe <isaac@mass-engineering.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/misc/armchina-npu/sky1/sky1.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/armchina-npu/sky1/sky1.c b/drivers/misc/armchina-npu/sky1/sky1.c
index 80daab0..879a543 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/armchina-npu/sky1/sky1.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/armchina-npu/sky1/sky1.c
@@ -380,6 +380,23 @@ static int sky1_npu_probe(struct platform_device *p_dev)
 				break;
 
 			cix_aipu_priv->pd_core[i] = bus_find_device_by_fwnode(&platform_bus_type, child);
+			if (!cix_aipu_priv->pd_core[i]) {
+				/*
+				 * A core declared with _ADR only (no _HID) has no
+				 * platform device: use its ACPI device instead. The
+				 * binding is kept across a module reload.
+				 */
+				struct acpi_device *adev = to_acpi_device_node(child);
+
+				if (!ACPI_COMPANION(&adev->dev)) {
+					ret = acpi_bind_one(&adev->dev, adev);
+					if (ret) {
+						fwnode_handle_put(child);
+						return ret;
+					}
+				}
+				cix_aipu_priv->pd_core[i] = &adev->dev;
+			}
                 	pm_runtime_enable(cix_aipu_priv->pd_core[i]);
 			dev_pm_domain_attach(cix_aipu_priv->pd_core[i], true);
 			dev_pm_set_driver_flags(cix_aipu_priv->pd_core[i], DPM_FLAG_NO_DIRECT_COMPLETE);
@@ -464,6 +481,11 @@ static void sky1_npu_remove(struct platform_device *p_dev)
 
 	armchina_aipu_remove(p_dev);
 
+	if (has_acpi_companion(&p_dev->dev)) {
+		for (int i = 0; i < CIX_NPU_PD_NUM; i++)
+			pm_runtime_disable(cix_aipu_priv->pd_core[i]);
+	}
+
 	sky1_npu_detach_pd(&p_dev->dev, &sky1);
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_PM
-- 
2.39.5

